      players: '2-4 players; with 4, fixed partnerships across the table.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck.',
      equipment: 'Deck and score track.',
      dealing: 'Deal six cards to each player, then turn one card up for provisional trumps.',
    },
    turnFlow: 'After six cards each and a turned trump indicator, eldest hand may stand or beg. If begging is accepted, dealer runs three more cards each and turns again until trump suit changes. In play, highest trump wins a trick; if no trump is played, highest card of the led suit wins. Players with the led suit may either follow suit or play trump, but cannot throw a non-trump card of another suit when they could follow. Score hand points in order High, Low, Jack, Game; first side to target wins the game.',
